**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `constructor-unit-tests`: 

**How to implement.** What a recorded run is for, the session it belongs to and the notes a reviewer writes on it, as pure Domain data (001 §K '`Experiment` = one recorded run: … a role: `Science | Calibration | Dark | DriftCheck | Diagnostic | Ignored | Planned`; a session'; 001 §E 'notes on experiments, studies and fit runs live in their files'; .spec-md §3.17: case names take a second word; the S9.1 brief: a role with int wire tags, a session and notes). Nothing reads them before step 288. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S9.1. In `OpticalConstructor.Domain/Experiments.fs`, directly after `ExperimentId` (`Experiments.fs:ExperimentId`), in this order: (1) `ExperimentRole` = `ScienceRun` | `CalibrationRun` | `DarkRun` | `DriftCheckRun` | `DiagnosticRun` | `IgnoredRun` | `PlannedRun`. `member this.value : int` answers 1 to 7 in that order, its disk tag; `static member tryOfWire (tag : int) : ExperimentRole option` answers `None` for any other tag (AGENTS.md: a closed set's tag is an int, and no `Unknown*` case); `member this.text : string` answers `Science`, `Calibration`, `Dark`, `Drift check`, `Diagnostic`, `Ignored` and `Planned`; `static member all : ExperimentRole list` lists the seven in tag order. (2) `SessionName of string` with `.value`, the measurement session a run belongs to when the user sets it by hand (S11.1's study splits the rest at its Diagnostic runs): `static member tryCreate (text : string) : SessionName option` keeps the text as given and answers `None` for an empty or white-space text. (3) `ExperimentNotes of string` with `.value`, free text, and `static member none : ExperimentNotes` = `ExperimentNotes ""`. No other type, member or option is added. In `OpticalConstructor.Storage/CanonicalJson.fs`, `CanonicalJson.options` gains one converter for `ExperimentRole`, written as step 166's `KitStar` converter is and registered with the others before the `JsonFSharpConverter`: it writes the case's `value` and reads through `ExperimentRole.tryOfWire`, an unknown tag throwing `JsonException`, which the callers report as `MalformedJsonErr`. `SessionName` and `ExperimentNotes` keep the single-case form every other single-case union has, and nothing else in the options changes. Tests. `ExperimentProxyTests` gains `an experiment role round-trips its wire tag and renders its text`: the tags 1 to 7 in order, `tryOfWire` inverse to `value`, `None` for 0 and 8, the seven texts exactly as above and `all` in tag order; and `a session name keeps its text and refuses a blank one, and notes are free text`: `SessionName.tryCreate "Day 1 (morning)"` is `Some (SessionName "Day 1 (morning)")`, `""` and `"   "` are `None`, and `ExperimentNotes.none.value` is empty. In `CanonicalJsonTests` (steps 28, 166), `every closed set with an int tag is written as its tag and read back` also writes each `ExperimentRole` as its tag (`DarkRun` as `3`) and reads it back, and `an unknown disk tag is refused` also refuses the role tag 8 with `MalformedJsonErr`.

**Acceptance.** After roles, sessions and notes land, `ExperimentRole` MUST hold the seven run roles with int tags 1-7 read back by `tryOfWire` and written as their tag by `CanonicalJson.options`, `SessionName.tryCreate` MUST refuse a blank text and `ExperimentNotes` MUST be free text; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `an experiment role round-trips its wire tag and renders its text` and `a session name keeps its text and refuses a blank one, and notes are free text`, the count rising by 2, and the changed `every closed set with an int tag is written as its tag and read back` and `an unknown disk tag is refused`; and build, elevation and the sixteen s29 invariants MUST pass.
